      "message": "Is this setting both flags for both RO and RW builds? How is it only enabling the right flag for the correct build?\n\n----\n\nCan you also add the following console command to your build and include the output here:\n\n`common/system.c`\n```\nstatic int command_in_rw(int argc, const char **argv)\n{\n#if defined(SECTION_IS_RW)\n\tint section_is_rw \u003d 1;\n#else\n\tint section_is_rw \u003d 0;\n#endif\n\n\tccprintf(\"image_copy \u003d %d\\n\", system_get_image_copy());\n\tccprintf(\"SECTION_IS_RW \u003d %d\\n\", section_is_rw);\n\tccprintf(\"system_is_in_rw \u003d %d\\n\", system_is_in_rw());\n\n\treturn EC_SUCCESS;\n}\nDECLARE_CONSOLE_COMMAND(in_rw, command_in_rw,\n\t\t\tNULL,\n\t\t\t\"Output system RW status.\");\n```\n\nWe\u0027ll want to validate both cases:\n\n1. Flash on the EC, verify `SECTION_IS_RW` is not defined while running in RO.\n2. Jump to RW first (`sysjump RW`) and then run `in_rw` to verify `SECTION_IS_RW` is enabled correctly.\n\nYou\u0027ll probably want to build on it a bit more to validate `SECTION_IS_RO` is defined correctly (only for RO builds).",
